newer_upstream: v20260913-2ae1860
also_newer: v20260913-f21f099, v20260913-02df436
since: 2026-09-13
refs: urb-agents #827, #836

reason: >-
  Every merge under atlas-data/** retags, so artifacts appear whether or not anything a
  consumer reads has changed. atlas states the three merges since e0ef430 are
  documentation and a CI label fix, with no contract change. So holding is a decision
  rather than inertia — and the previous pin moved for two operator-visible public
  contract defects, which is the bar.

release_when: >-
  atlas says explicitly that a merge touches a contract, and nominates a tag. atlas has
  committed to saying so; silence means nothing a consumer reads has moved. Not on
  tidiness, and not merely because drift reports behind.

carry_forward: >-
  Two things that changed under this hold and apply to the next pin. First, uis-artifact.json
  now carries artifact_digest and image_digest explicitly, from v20260913-2ae1860 onward;
  atlas deliberately did NOT rename or revalue `digest`, because this repository reads it.
  verify-application-pin.sh now prefers artifact_digest, falls back to digest for artifacts
  published before the field existed, and fails if both exist and disagree. Second, the
  >= 1.6.69 version gate still applies unless atlas says otherwise, and the pass condition
  at install remains a silent _warn_unrendered_operational — which is the tester's evidence
  to produce, not this repository's.

